PS5: GPU compositing on Sony's GLES library (libSceGLSlimVSH)

Applies after every earlier patch (it also touches files of 0013).
The shell starts GLSlim in the WebProcess (src/ps5/glslim) and sets
PROSPEROWEB_GPU_READY=1; WebProcessPlayStation then makes a shared display
on it. GLContext uses pbuffer contexts (GLSlim cannot make a surfaceless one
current) and ends frames with the shell's frame end. TextureMapper's programs
come from the console's own precompiled binaries (no GLSL compiler). The
compositor draws into an FBO; each frame is read back and sent to the UI
process as an ordinary Update, which it acknowledges with DisplayDidRefresh,
so the UI process and WKPagePaint are unchanged. The main thread never
touches GL (GLSlim aborts when a second context is made current on another
thread): BitmapTexturePool's timer no longer borrows the sharing context,
and the compositor thread releases unused pool textures itself.

With Mesa instead (src/ps5/mesa, EVO Player as the GPU owner,
ps5_mesa_active()): surfaceless contexts, no frame end, and TextureMapper's
own GLSL is compiled; the FBO, readback and Update path is shared.

